# What is SSL?

SSL = **Secure Sockets Layer**

It was the original protocol used to secure internet communication.

Today:

❌ SSL is obsolete.

Modern websites use **TLS (Transport Layer Security)** instead.

However, people still commonly say "SSL certificate" even though most sites actually use TLS.

---

# What is TLS?

TLS encrypts data sent between:

```text
Your Browser

↓

Internet

↓

Website Server
```

Without TLS:

Anyone intercepting the traffic may be able to read sensitive information if no other protections exist.

With TLS:

The intercepted traffic appears encrypted and unreadable without the session keys.

---

# What is HTTPS?

HTTP = Normal communication

HTTPS = HTTP + TLS encryption

Example:

```text
http://example.com
```

❌ Not encrypted

---

```text
https://example.com
```

✅ Encrypted

Always prefer HTTPS for sensitive communication.

